# Issue commit linking

Every **task-related** commit must reference both trackers in the **commit body** so Linear links commits, the GitHub **Development** panel links correctly, and GitHub issues auto-close on merge to `main`.

**Issue keys never go in the commit subject** — keep subjects clean: `<type>(<scope>): <summary>` only.

## Required subject format

```
<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>
```

| Part | Rule |
|---|---|
| `<type>` | Conventional Commits: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf` |
| `<scope>` | Allowed scopes from `01-git-workflow.mdc` (`bookmarks`, `auth`, `billing`, `go`, …) |
| Summary | Imperative mood; whole subject ≤72 chars |
| **Forbidden in subject** | `[SB-N]`, `[#N]`, `(#N)`, `SB-N`, or any issue key |

## Required body format (new Linear-tracked work)

The commit body must include **both** closing lines — one per tracker:

```
fixes SB-N
fixes #N
```

Place each on its own line. Use the synced pair for the leaf issue (`SB-42` ↔ `#612`).

- `fixes SB-N` → Linear commit linking (In Progress on push; Done on `main` per team automations)
- `fixes #N` → GitHub auto-close on merge to `main` + Development panel

## Epic (parent) issues

Subtasks under a parent epic follow the same rules, with **parent auto-close only on the final in-scope child**.

| Commit | Subject | Body |
|---|---|---|
| Any subtask under a parent | key-free | `fixes SB-<leaf>` + `fixes #<leaf>` |
| **Final** child of parent P | key-free | leaf lines + one `fixes SB-<P>` + `fixes #<P>` per parent in `CLOSE_PARENTS` |
| Atomic leaf (no parent) | key-free | `fixes SB-<leaf>` + `fixes #<leaf>` |
| Roadmap-only | `[P*-*]` allowed in subject | no `fixes` lines |

**Do not** put parent `fixes` lines on intermediate subtasks.

The orchestrator passes `CLOSE_PARENTS: linear=[SB-P, …] github=[#P, …] | none`. Execution agents **must not guess**.

```bash
# GOOD — intermediate subtask under epic SB-8 / #8
feat(auth): add sign-in shell

fixes SB-11
fixes #11

# GOOD — last in-scope child of epic SB-8 / #8
feat(auth): add MFA challenge screen

fixes SB-12
fixes #12
fixes SB-8
fixes #8

# BAD — keys in subject
feat(auth)[SB-11][#11]: add sign-in shell

# BAD — missing GitHub line
feat(auth): add sign-in shell

fixes SB-11

# BAD — premature epic close
fixes SB-11
fixes #11
fixes SB-8
fixes #8
```

**Verifier FAIL** when Linear sync was in scope:

- Body missing `fixes SB-<leaf>` or `fixes #<leaf>`
- Subject contains `[SB-N]`, `[#N]`, or bare `SB-N` / `#N` as issue keys
- Body includes parent `fixes` when parent is **not** in `CLOSE_PARENTS`
- Body missing parent `fixes` when parent **is** in `CLOSE_PARENTS`

### Issue key precedence

1. **Linear + GitHub pair** — `SB-N` + `#N` when task exists on SlugBase team (orchestrator LINEAR SYNC, user named `SB-N` or `#N`)
2. **Roadmap only** — `[P2-01]` in subject when no tracker issue exists yet
3. **Legacy GitHub-only** — body-only `fixes #N` (no Linear issue); subject key-free

### Examples

```bash
# GOOD — Linear-tracked work
feat(auth): add server-side session store with configurable TTL

fixes SB-12
fixes #612

# GOOD — roadmap-only (no tracker issue)
feat(workspaces)[P2-01]: implement workspace creation with entitlement check

# GOOD — legacy GitHub-only (no Linear issue yet)
feat(auth): add session store

fixes #12

# BAD — keys in subject (old format)
feat(auth)[#12]: add session store

# BAD — no closing keywords in body
feat(auth): add session store
```

## Auto-close on merge

GitHub auto-closes issues referenced with `fixes #N`, `closes #N`, or `resolves #N` in the commit body when merged to `main`. Linear links via `fixes SB-N` in the body per the GitHub commit-linking webhook.

## Exceptions (no issue key required)

- Pure repo hygiene: `chore(repo): init pnpm workspace`
- Integration merge commits: `chore(repo): integrate orchestrator batch (<BATCH_ID>)` — body may reference batch issues if needed

## Enforcement

- **Execution agents:** key-free subject; body `fixes SB-<leaf>` + `fixes #<leaf>`; parent lines only per `CLOSE_PARENTS`
- **Verifiers:** Layer 3 — FAIL on missing body lines, keys in subject, or epic parent mismatches
- **Orchestrator prompts:** pass `LINEAR_KEY`, `GITHUB_NUMBER`, and `CLOSE_PARENTS` in the GIT block; see `.cursor/skills/orchestrator/prompt-templates.md`
